From: rufus159 <rufus159@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: restore thermal protection, drop empty u-boot-env layout

Three fixes for GL-MT5000, all verified against the running device.

1) CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL + CONFIG_CPU_IDLE

filogic already sets CONFIG_CPU_THERMAL=y and the DTS carries a full
cooling-maps block (cpu-passive plus three cpu-active maps bound to all
four cores, trips at 85/115/117/120/125 C), but the generic config
leaves CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL unset. Without it cpufreq never registers
a cooling device, so:

  /sys/class/thermal/cooling_device*      -> empty
  thermal_zone_bind_cooling_device        -> not in kallsyms
  cpufreq_cooling_register                -> not in kallsyms

and the box happily sits at 92 C at full load (measured, 4x busy loop)
without ever throttling. Turning the option on makes the existing
cooling-maps actually do something.

CONFIG_CPU_IDLE is also off, which is why there is no
/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpuidle directory at all. Enable it plus the
menu and teo governors so idle states can be used once the DTS describes
them.

Note on what this does NOT fix: idle temperature is 77-78 C and stays
there even with all four cores locked to 500 MHz for 40 s, so the bulk of
the heat is the RTL8366UB switch and the three 2.5G PHYs, not the CPU.
Thermal protection is a safety net, not a temperature reduction.

2) CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_U_BOOT_ENV off

The DTS declares a u-boot-env partition with nvmem-layout
compatible = "u-boot,env". That partition is all zeroes on this board
(the vendor firmware never wrote it), so the layout driver rejects it:

  u-boot-env-layout ...: Invalid calculated CRC32: 0xc09e9b4c (expected: 0x00000000)
  probe with driver u-boot-env-layout failed with error -22

Nothing depends on it (no uboot-envtools in the image, fw_printenv is
absent), so the layout driver is pure noise here. Turning it off removes
the two dmesg error lines. This is the kernel option rather than dropping
the DTS node so other filogic boards that do carry a real env keep theirs.

Signed-off-by: rufus159 <rufus159@users.noreply.github.com>
---

diff --git a/target/linux/generic/config-6.18 b/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
--- a/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
@@ -1107,14 +1107,14 @@
 # CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_SCHEDUTIL is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_USERSPACE is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL is not set
-# CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL is not set
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL=y
 # CONFIG_CPU_HOTPLUG_STATE_CONTROL is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_ICACHE_DISABLE is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_ICACHE_MISMATCH_WORKAROUND is not set
-# CONFIG_CPU_IDLE is not set
+CONFIG_CPU_IDLE=y
 # CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_LADDER is not set
-# CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_MENU is not set
-# CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_TEO is not set
+CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_MENU=y
+CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_TEO=y
 # CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_MULTIPLE_DRIVERS is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_ISOLATION is not set
 # CONFIG_CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN is not set
diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.18 b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.18
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.18
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@
 CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUTS=y
 CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_ADTRAN=y
 CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_ASCII_ENV=y
-CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_U_BOOT_ENV=y
+# CONFIG_NVMEM_LAYOUT_U_BOOT_ENV is not set
 CONFIG_NVMEM_MTK_EFUSE=y
 CONFIG_NVMEM_SYSFS=y
 CONFIG_OF=y
